# SRG-APP-000427-WSR-000186  -  CAT II
# The web server must only accept client certificates (user and machine)
# issued by DOD PKI or DOD-approved PKI Certificate Authorities (CAs).
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000427-WSR-000186
group:           V-206430
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-002470
control_rev5:    SC-23

contribution:    Splunk Web can perform PKI-based user authentication itself: it can
                 require a client certificate, validate it against a nominated root
                 certificate authority store, and extract the user identity from a named
                 field of the certificate. On the splunkd side, client certificates can be
                 required of the machines that connect. The identity of the certificate's
                 issuer is not visible to configuration.

governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] enableCertBasedUserAuth equals true
check:           web.conf [settings] requireClientCert equals true
check:           web.conf [settings] sslRootCAPath non_empty
check:           web.conf [settings] certBasedUserAuthMethod in CommonName|EDIPI|PIV
check:           server.conf [sslConfig] requireClientCert equals true
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] requireClientCert https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] certBasedUserAuthMethod https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
vendor:          web.conf [settings] enableCertBasedUserAuth https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
vendor:          web.conf [settings] requireClientCert https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
vendor:          web.conf [settings] sslRootCAPath https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Whether the accepted client certificates were issued by an approved
                 certificate authority - established by inspecting the trust anchor with
                 openssl on the host operating system per the SPLK-CL-000450 check text;
                 configuration names the store, not its issuers
external:        Certificate revocation checking, including the CRL files the instance
                 reads from its auth/crl directory - the issuing PKI and its revocation
                 service (see server.conf.spec:1125-1143, certificateStatusValidationMethod
                 = crl)
external:        Issuance and distribution of user and machine certificates - the approved
                 public key infrastructure
external:        Where PKI user authentication is performed by a fronting proxy or a SAML
                 identity provider rather than by Splunk Web, certificate validation is
                 that component's and the SRG's own not-applicable clause governs -
                 identity provider or reverse proxy configuration
external:        Mapping of the extracted certificate identity to a user and roles in the
                 directory service - directory service configuration

citation:        web.conf.spec:120-131 (enableCertBasedUserAuth = <boolean>, default false;
                 "When this setting has a value of 'true', 'requireClientCert' must *also*
                 have a value of 'true'"); web.conf.spec:133-142 (certBasedUserAuthMethod,
                 values CommonName, EDIPI and PIV, no default); web.conf.spec:144-149
                 (certBasedUserAuthPivOidList); web.conf.spec:151-167 (requireClientCert,
                 default false; a client can connect only if it presents a certificate
                 signed by the same CA, and when certificate-based user authentication is
                 on the root CA in web.conf's sslRootCAPath is used); web.conf.spec:108-114
                 (sslRootCAPath, used when both requireClientCert and
                 enableCertBasedUserAuth are true); server.conf.spec:858-874 ([sslConfig]
                 requireClientCert, default false; deployment clients must present
                 certificates before they can poll for configurations or applications);
                 product STIG SPLK-CL-000450 fix and check text for the certificate files
                 and issuer verification
finding:         Splunk is not configured to validate client certificates to the extent the
                 product allows: certificate-based user authentication is not enabled,
                 client certificates are not required on the Splunk Web or splunkd
                 listener, the root certificate authority store is unset, or no documented
                 identity extraction method is configured.
